-- The New Zealand rates rebate of rates-rebate-buggy.l4 and
-- rates-rebate-fixed.l4, both forms in one file, with the FLOOR taken out of
-- the income excess: it is $1 for every $8, fractions included.
-- The deck's own comment on the FLOOR in the OpenFisca code: "non legislative
-- and only to conform output of variable with existing infrastracture".
--
-- Why this file exists: "the rebate does not rise when income rises" is the
-- first assertion a tester would write, and it holds of the BUGGY form too, so
-- it cannot find the bug.
-- `l4 prove` says so here, with the FLOOR out, in a fraction of a second.
-- With the FLOOR in, adding the same assertion to rates-rebate-buggy.l4 gives
-- `unknown (timeout)` from z3 4.16.0, at the default 10 seconds and at
-- `--timeout 120` alike, while the fixed form is proved in under a second.
-- A test must not depend on a solver's patience, so that case is not a
-- fixture.
-- The assertion that does find the bug is the ceiling, last in this file.
--
-- The helpers are top-level rules and not WHERE bindings on purpose: at the
-- commit this was written, `l4 prove` crashed on a WHERE binding that takes no
-- parameters.
IMPORT prelude

GIVETH A NUMBER
`income threshold` MEANS 25180

GIVETH A NUMBER
`additional per dependant` MEANS 500

GIVETH A NUMBER
`initial contribution` MEANS 160

GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum allowable` MEANS 630

GIVEN dependants IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`allowable income` dependants MEANS
  `income threshold` PLUS dependants TIMES `additional per dependant`

GIVEN rates IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rates excess` rates MEANS max 0 (rates MINUS `initial contribution`)

GIVEN rates      IS A NUMBER
      income     IS A NUMBER
      dependants IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`buggy rebate` rates income dependants MEANS
  max 0
    (min rates
      (min (((2 TIMES `rates excess` rates) DIVIDED BY 3)
              MINUS ((income MINUS `allowable income` dependants) DIVIDED BY 8))
           `maximum allowable`))

GIVEN rates      IS A NUMBER
      income     IS A NUMBER
      dependants IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`fixed rebate` rates income dependants MEANS
  max 0
    (min rates
      (min (((2 TIMES `rates excess` rates) DIVIDED BY 3)
              MINUS ((max 0 (income MINUS `allowable income` dependants)) DIVIDED BY 8))
           `maximum allowable`))

§ `Any ratepayer`
    GIVEN rates      IS A NUMBER
          income     IS A NUMBER
          dependants IS A NUMBER
          later      IS A NUMBER

-- proved: the buggy form never pays more as income rises
#ASSERT later AT LEAST income IMPLIES `buggy rebate` rates later dependants AT MOST `buggy rebate` rates income dependants

-- proved: nor does the fixed form
#ASSERT later AT LEAST income IMPLIES `fixed rebate` rates later dependants AT MOST `fixed rebate` rates income dependants

-- refuted: the ceiling finds what monotonicity could not
#ASSERT `buggy rebate` rates income dependants AT MOST (2 TIMES `rates excess` rates) DIVIDED BY 3

-- proved
#ASSERT `fixed rebate` rates income dependants AT MOST (2 TIMES `rates excess` rates) DIVIDED BY 3
